Sval: closing the selected tab returns to the tab the user saw last

Firefox returns to the closed tab's opener while it is visible, and
otherwise to its neighbour in the tab strip. Sval's tab strip is hidden
and its order is not the panel's, so the neighbour is any tab of the
Workspace, often one inside a group the user never opened. A pin's page
is hidden whenever another tab is selected, so it is never a visible
opener either. SvalTabAfterClose picks the tab the user saw last among
the Workspace's tabs and its pins' pages.
browser_tabSuccessors.js asserts Firefox's neighbour rule, so its
expected tab follows Sval's.

diff --git a/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js b/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
--- a/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
+++ b/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
@@ -6315,12 +6315,12 @@
         return aTab.successor;
       }

-      if (
-        aTab.owner?.visible &&
-        !excludeTabs.has(aTab.owner) &&
-        Services.prefs.getBoolPref("browser.tabs.selectOwnerOnClose")
-      ) {
-        return aTab.owner;
+      // Sval: the tab the user saw last in the Workspace (SvalTabAfterClose).
+      let lastSeen = ChromeUtils.importESModule(
+        "moz-src:///browser/components/sval/SvalTabAfterClose.sys.mjs"
+      ).tabAfterClose(aTab, excludeTabs);
+      if (lastSeen) {
+        return lastSeen;
       }

       // Try to find a remaining tab that comes after the given tab
